<SddModule keywords="module, authoring, decomposition, entity, dbc, sdd-new, sdd-check" type="directive" ver="2.4">
  <Mission>
    Materialize the smallest cohesive module hierarchy from an actual scope draft. The autonomous
    route is skeleton → orient → one whole-document Write → soft check → handoff. Tasks belong to
    scaffold; dialogue ceremony belongs to the optional interactive profile.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState deps="AX_TOOL_INVOCATION, AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH">
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-tool-invocation"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-progressive-disclosure"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-refine-module-preserves-contracts"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-artifact-style-self-check"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <Contracts>
    {{> "contract/process/deviation-record-format"}}
  </Contracts>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_CREATE">
      <Goal>Create actual module artifacts first.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Resolve initial/add/refine from disk once. For each new cohesive module, call the ToolCall
        before reading optional formats. A function/fix scope creates one Function/Service module
        without invented Port or parallel owner.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="moduleManifest">npx gennady sdd-new module --scope <scope> --module <module></ToolCall> Inputs <scope>, <module>: scope and cohesive module name resolved in this step. Use moduleManifest.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_1_ORIENT">
      <Goal>Reuse existing ownership and dependencies.</Goal>
      <Action>
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="orientation">npx gennady sdd-orient <module-spec-path></ToolCall> Inputs <module-spec-path>: exact created path from the STEP_0_CREATE moduleManifest, or the existing module spec path read in that step. Use orientation before portal registration.
        `sdd-orient` is the only unconditional foreign-context read. Depth here is proportional to
        the confirmed SCALE, never self-assessed (`AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH`):
        <LogicSwitch on="SCALE and orientation ambiguity">
        - WHEN SCALE is `fix` or `function` AND orientation exposes no real ambiguity -> EXPRESS:
          skip interview, research, and registry protocols entirely — no gate is dropped,
          STEP_4_CHECK and STEP_5_CLOSE still run in full.
        - WHEN SCALE is `product`, or orientation exposes a real ambiguity -> load interview,
          research, or registry protocols as needed.
        </LogicSwitch>
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_2_FILL">
      <Goal>Generate and write the complete module specification once.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Retain every SECTION marker. Replace every guidance/instructional comment with authored
        content; remove all such comments before Write. Keep a closed inventory, one owner for
        shared files/errors, public surfaces, per-operation DbC, file structure, and negative behavior.
        The scope owns its requirement IDs. With no narrower obligation write
        `No module-specific requirements. Implements parent requirements: <IDs>.`
        A disputed autonomous boundary choice is one module Decision Log line per
        `DEVIATION_RECORD_FORMAT`; a zero-new-information decision continues without a dialogue stop.
        Per `AX_REFINE_MODULE_PRESERVES_CONTRACTS`, removing a public entity or weakening a
        postcondition is a breaking change: it needs a Decision Log entry with operator-confirmed
        `Risk accepted` plus a Pivot Invalidation List naming every consumer module (the siblings
        whose Inter-Module Dependencies edge points at this one) as a `refine-module` target.
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/pivot-formats.xml")` gives the list format.
        `Edit`, `Patch`, and per-section writes are forbidden in authoring.

        Action → expected observation (notation, not shell):
          Read on-disk skeleton once → skeleton.
          Compose COMPLETE module in memory → full draft:
            while filling entity-inventory, entity-surface, or DbC:
              read format only from that owning section's comments, at that moment → section format.
          Before writing, run the self-check pass per `AX_ARTIFACT_STYLE_SELF_CHECK` → pre-write check done.
          exactly ONE whole-file Write → skeleton replaced with the composed document.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_3_RECONCILE_MAP">
      <Goal>Make the scope Module Map match actual module files.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Validate that the scope's already generated whole document names the exact relative module
        links and dependency direction. Do not patch its Module Map here: the scope writer owns that
        map, and authoring never creates a second sectional writer.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_4_CHECK">
      <Goal>Consume mechanical draft receipts.</Goal>
      <Action>
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="moduleReceipt">npx gennady sdd-check --spec <module-spec-path> --authoring</ToolCall> Inputs <module-spec-path>: exact path from moduleManifest. Use moduleReceipt.
        The receipt auto-fixes trivial format. If a content hint remains, report authoring incomplete;
        never switch to sectional Edit/Patch repair. Rerun once only after checker auto-fix for the
        final receipt. For scale=function|fix, check
        the scope and its one module in this same pass and treat both receipts as one manifest result.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <ScalePath when="scale=function|fix">
      One Function/Service module without invented Port/Adapter; one authoring pass, one combined
      manifest, no repeated boundary discussion.
    </ScalePath>

    <Step id="STEP_5_CLOSE">
      <Goal>Make module authoring completion durable.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Only after the final moduleReceipt has no hints, close authoring atomically.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="moduleAuthoringReceipt">npx gennady sdd-log &lt;module-spec-path&gt; authoring-complete</ToolCall> Inputs &lt;module-spec-path&gt;: exact checked path from STEP_4_CHECK. Use moduleAuthoringReceipt.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_6_HANDOFF">
      <Goal>Leave an actual checked hierarchy.</Goal>
      <Action>
        If an operator explicitly requested live interaction, lazily
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/authoring-interactive.directive.xml")`.
        Otherwise record deviations and continue to the mechanical close/scaffold route.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>
</SddModule>
